S3AFUEL V1.7 - READ.ME file
----------------------------

Welcome to my Fuel Consumption program V1.7.  Please note this file is for New Users only.  Users upgrading from V1.5 should read README.V15.  V1.6 users should read README.V16

The archive should contain the following files:

S3AFUEL7.APP        Main program

S3AFUELH.OVL        Optional Help file
S3AFUELP.OVL        Optional Print file
S3APRINT.DYL        Optional Print file

README.NEW          'Get you started' instructions for new users
README.V15          Upgrade instructions for present users of V1.5
README.V16          Upgrade instructions for present users of V1.6

HISTORY.TXT         Details of the various upgrades the program has gone through.

REGISTER.TXT        Details on how to register the program.
LICENCE.TXT         A legal document

S3AFUEL7.TXT        Full instructions in ASCII Text format

I would strongly encourage you to read the instructions, but if you still insist on flying blind:

1.   Put S3AFUEL7.APP in your \APP\ directory

2.   If you want to use the optional On-Line Help (Highly recommended) put the file S3AFUELH.OVL into an \APP\S3AFUEL\ directory.

3.   If you want to use the optional Print option put the file S3AFUELP.OVL into the \APP\S3AFUEL\ directory and the file S3APRINT.DYL into an \OPD\ directory.  Note that this file is common to all my programs, so if you have more than one of them you only need one copy of this file.

4.   Install (PSION-I) and go for it !!

If you do get a problem, PLEASE read the full instructions.  I have yet to be asked a question that wasn't already fully explained in the instructions !!

All comments, and registrations, still gratefully received.

If you wish to register, up-to-date details are in the file REGISTER.TXT

If you want to monitor progress on upgrades and enhancements, as well as see if any bugs have been reported, visit the home page on the World-Wide Web. The address is :  

	http://ourworld.compuserve.com/homepages/alanrichey
	or
	http://members.aol.com/alanrichey

Also, if you like the look of this program, why not have a look at my other programs.  A full list is as follows:

    S3ATASKx.ZIP    :  An Extended Task (ToDo) Manager.
    S3ADRAWx.ZIP    :  A Drawing/Icon Viewer/Editor.
    S3ACOLLx.ZIP    :  A Collection (Records, Books, Stamps etc) Manager.
    S3ABANKx.ZIP    :  A Personal Accounts package that includes all of the
                       following smaller programs as optional modules.
    S3AHOMEx.ZIP    :  A Home Inventory program based on the Quicken version.
    S3APLANx.ZIP    :  A Budget Planner based on the Quicken Financial Planner.
    S3AFUELx.ZIP    :  A Fuel Consumption Monitor.
    S3AINVx.ZIP     :  An Investment Tracking Program.
    S3AEXPx.ZIP     :  An Expense Account Monitor.

All of these programs also run on the S3C.

With the exception of S3ATASK, these programs are also available for the Siena, and just use the prefix 'SNA' rather than 'S3A, i.e. SNABANKx.ZIP
                                                                    
('x' denotes a version number)

